# JSDoc Standards

## Language

Documentation is written in **Brazilian Portuguese**, matching existing entity and facade docs.

## Class-Level Block

Every entity class and `Bling` includes:

- One-line description of the resource/module.
- `@see` link to the Bling reference section for that resource.

Reference: class header in `src/entities/camposCustomizados/index.ts`, `src/entities/nfes/index.ts`, `src/bling.ts`.

## Method-Level Block

Each public entity method documents:

1. **Description** — what the operation does.
2. **`@param`** — for each argument; use `{Type}` and Portuguese description.
3. **`@returns`** — `{Promise<...>}` with brief note if empty (`Não há retorno`).
4. **`@throws {BlingApiException|BlingInternalException}`** — on methods that call the repository.
5. **`@see`** — deep link to the specific Bling API operation URL.

For parameterless methods, omit `@param`. For optional params, note optionality in the description. Orchestrators such as `Homologacao.execute()` may omit `@throws` when they only delegate.

## Repository & Exceptions

- Repository public methods use `@inheritDoc` where overriding interface (`src/repositories/bling.repository.ts`).
- Private methods document `@param`, `@returns`, `@throws` when non-obvious (`defaultCatchBehavior`).
- Exception classes document purpose and constructor params (`src/exceptions/bling-api.exception.ts`).

## Property Tags

Use `@property` on class fields when documenting internal state in repository (`src/repositories/bling.repository.ts`, `src/repositories/bling-in-memory.repository.ts`).

## `@example` on Facade

`Bling` class includes a minimal `@example` in `src/bling.ts` — preserve this pattern for the main entry only; entity classes do not need `@example` blocks.

## Interfaces

Domain `types/` JSDoc lists each enum value. Interface field JSDoc is optional. Document operation behavior on the entity method.

## Links

Base reference: `https://developer.bling.com.br/referencia`

Use URL-encoded resource names as in existing `@see` tags (`src/entities/contatos/index.ts`).
